{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1152403-nom-nom-nom","id":1152403,"title":"Nom nom nom","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-23T21:32:06-07:00","id":1152403,"title":"Nom nom nom","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">There area number of ways that one can devour another as a means to gain dread power. If you are willing to cross that moral event horizon there are a number of shortcuts to power that to require another to pay the final price. From anthropophagy, skin taking, blood bathing, body thievery, to the rites of Hecate, and heart harvesting diablery of the sons of Phobos; power can be had. I\u2019m sure I am missing some others, no doubt there are ways to permanently eat ghosts, spirits and souls to get power. </span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">A <b>devour</b>er can be a terrible villain. In some cases, like when the prey is more monstrous* the horrific nature of these acts seems more palatable. After all you were going to kill that thing anyways, why not take every part of the monster..</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Possible ideas. </span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">A devourer kills and consumes monster after monster, person after person, gaining more and more powers as they go. This would be a way to have a Boss NPC that may have started out as a mortal long ago. As far as I can tell there is nothing stopping a full template from the feast either. </span></span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">A group of devourers joins forces to share in the hunt, and teach each other their craft. This arrangement probably won\u2019t last for long however the carnage that could be wrought in that time would be terrible.</span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Reskinning act of devouring to be more \u2018palatable\u2019: </span></span></b><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">An alchemist extracts golden exudation full of promise from a subject. A Mad Scientist or doctor could learns the secrets and then harvests certain components from the blood and heart of the vampire on their slab. An occultist could \u2018trap the essence\u2019 of a monster rather than eating a pound of it\u2019s flesh.</span></span></b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18291-unrepentantweed","name":"Unrepentantweed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T00:36:51-07:00","id":1152423,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting theme, but how can we use it? Of course, the simplest route is to have an NPC acquiring Dread Powers from the feast. But what other, more specific twists, can we add to it?<br /> <br /> A Slasher Undertaking could be linked to the devourer. Either of them could work, each painting the character in a new light. I think I'll work it on a chronicle myself.<br /> <br /> Vampires could have a Bloodline and/or Coil of the Dragon devoted to eating the flesh of the living. Since anthropophagy is already a Vampire theme, it does need the extra mileage of flesh and unavoidable death to work, though.<br /> <br /> Werewolves already do take advantage from this, but a secret Gift or Ritual could enhance and further the effect.<br /> <br /> Mages also can use this in several ways. But maybe a twist on the Tremere Lich can make it easier to take the power by indulging in the flesh instead of soul.<br /> <br /> Changelings could have Contracts of Flesh that use human meat as a catch.<br /> <br /> Everyone can benefit of some thematic Merits or Conditions.<br /> <br /> I'll work on this as soon as I have time. I had been out of this forums for too much time, already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T04:58:13-07:00","id":1152469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1152403-nom-nom-nom?p=1152423#post1152423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting theme, but how can we use it? Of course, the simplest route is to have an NPC acquiring Dread Powers from the feast. But what other, more specific twists, can we add to it?<br /> <br /> A Slasher Undertaking could be linked to the devourer. Either of them could work, each painting the character in a new light. I think I'll work it on a chronicle myself.<br /> <br /> Vampires could have a Bloodline and/or Coil of the Dragon devoted to eating the flesh of the living. Since anthropophagy is already a Vampire theme, it does need the extra mileage of flesh and unavoidable death to work, though.<br /> <br /> Werewolves already do take advantage from this, but a secret Gift or Ritual could enhance and further the effect.<br /> <br /> Mages also can use this in several ways. But maybe a twist on the Tremere Lich can make it easier to take the power by indulging in the flesh instead of soul.<br /> <br /> Changelings could have Contracts of Flesh that use human meat as a catch.<br /> <br /> Everyone can benefit of some thematic Merits or Conditions.<br /> <br /> I'll work on this as soon as I have time. I had been out of this forums for too much time, already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire: since vamps are, as you said, already into human consumption, it would need to be escalated. Maybe soul eating as well?<br /> <br /> Werewolf: they already have incentive to eat people too. Maybe binding their souls in a sick parody of Renown brands? Or using Idigam Essence Shaping trick to create Soul Slaves, or regurgitate consumed spirits into Magath?<br /> <br /> Mages: if souls are composed of the Subtle Arcana, maybe bodies have links to the Gross Arcana? I could see a very witch-y Legacy (with a cauldron) that stews bodies into potions to enhance their magic or take something from the Victim - Youth (Time), beauty or strength (Life), or their relationships (Space). Not sure how Matter or Forces would play out though.<br /> <br /> Changeling: with Contracts broken up into Regalia, I could see a Goblin Contract or Entitlement based around substituting eating certain body parts in place of an entire Regalia's Loopholes. Arms for Swords, Brains for Crowns, etc.<br /> <br /> Promethean: You might be able to harvest Pyros from people, similar to Sublimati, though this is strictly Centimani territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T02:00:45-07:00","id":1152733,"title":"","content":"It seems good, lets go further:<br /> <br /> Vampire: by eating the flesh, those vamps reach the Soul. Surviving victims get two Conditions, Flesh Scarred indicates the heinous wounds that can't heal completely, maybe coupled with Crippled or similar. Soul Scarred, though, is what will bound the victim eternally to the monster. A completely eaten victim could grant the vampire the Engorged Condition, to be shed for temporary access to a mental or physical quality of the victim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T03:35:54-07:00","id":1152743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1152403-nom-nom-nom?p=1152733#post1152733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems good, lets go further:<br /> <br /> Vampire: by eating the flesh, those vamps reach the Soul. Surviving victims get two Conditions, Flesh Scarred indicates the heinous wounds that can't heal completely, maybe coupled with Crippled or similar. Soul Scarred, though, is what will bound the victim eternally to the monster. A completely eaten victim could grant the vampire the Engorged Condition, to be shed for temporary access to a mental or physical quality of the victim.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. For something slightly different, what about instead of taking chunks out, they hollow the victim out like a spider draining it's prey? Still consuming the same body mass, but distinctly looks weirder and fits with the &quot;vampire bites suck&quot; thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T13:19:05-07:00","id":1152898,"title":"","content":"It could go both ways, with the vampire choosing between them. Maybe the distinction could be just one of time, with the dissolution of a given mass being slower than just taking out flesh without further care.<br /> <br /> Werewolves could have a ritual to bind the very soul of an eaten human. It could be used to make Fetishes, or otherwise turn the soul into a Spirit, an ephemeral being it was never meant to be. It would be a Magath of a Ghost with a kind of Spirit defined by the Uratha. Maybe it could feed the human soul to their Totem, or other spirit linked to the pack.<br /> <br /> For Mages, I can think of so many distinct ways to use human flesh that I prefer to narrow a little. A Legacy based on the act of consumption itself, either raw or a stew, but no potions. It could drain small and temporary quantities of the victim's Traits, without the need of much more time or preparation. I don't know, I'm still thinking that straight, but I like the idea of the cannibal hag for once, I would just keep with flesh instead of potions.<br /> <br /> Unless it is a last attainment to produce foods and other things to give other people. Lets not forget the theme of the unwanted cannibal.<br /> <br /> Changelings could also have also eating-based Oaths. I can picture the giant that swear to eat Jack being able to find out trespassers out of having an Oath to eat'em, or the fabled warning of not eating fairy food being added with a little &quot;spice&quot;, like in a tale I heard once about a barrel of wine, gift from a Troll King to a peasant, a delicious wine that never ceased, but the peasant should never open the barrel. When the peasant opens to look into the wine, there are rotten corpses inside.<br /> <br /> There is no reason for other Refinements to learn how to harvest something from human bodies. Prometheans are natural alchemical furnaces, and humanity is their goal. To process actual humans in several ways seems hardly out of theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T15:46:22-07:00","id":1152962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1152403-nom-nom-nom?p=1152898#post1152898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could go both ways, with the vampire choosing between them. Maybe the distinction could be just one of time, with the dissolution of a given mass being slower than just taking out flesh without further care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or 2 separate (but conceptually related) Bloodlines. One has savage fangs and gets their blood with a side of meat, the other are spiders in human form, turning prey into desiccated husks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1152403-nom-nom-nom?p=1152898#post1152898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves could have a ritual to bind the very soul of an eaten human. It could be used to make Fetishes, or otherwise turn the soul into a Spirit, an ephemeral being it was never meant to be. It would be a Magath of a Ghost with a kind of Spirit defined by the Uratha. Maybe it could feed the human soul to their Totem, or other spirit linked to the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds very Bale Hound, I'm just saying. &quot;<i>Blood and Souls for my lord Thurifuge!</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1152403-nom-nom-nom?p=1152898#post1152898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Mages, I can think of so many distinct ways to use human flesh that I prefer to narrow a little. A Legacy based on the act of consumption itself, either raw or a stew, but no potions. It could drain small and temporary quantities of the victim's Traits, without the need of much more time or preparation. I don't know, I'm still thinking that straight, but I like the idea of the cannibal hag for once, I would just keep with flesh instead of potions.<br /> <br /> Unless it is a last attainment to produce foods and other things to give other people. Lets not forget the theme of the unwanted cannibal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just meant cooking people. Meat, broth, whatever. As a Legacy, I don't know what the Arcana would be. Again, Life, Time, and Space are easy options for theft. As for the &quot;gift baskets&quot;, just make it a later Attainment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1152403-nom-nom-nom?p=1152898#post1152898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings could also have also eating-based Oaths. I can picture the giant that swear to eat Jack being able to find out trespassers out of having an Oath to eat'em, or the fabled warning of not eating fairy food being added with a little &quot;spice&quot;, like in a tale I heard once about a barrel of wine, gift from a Troll King to a peasant, a delicious wine that never ceased, but the peasant should never open the barrel. When the peasant opens to look into the wine, there are rotten corpses inside.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<i>I do so solemnly swear to grind the bones of any intruders to make my bread.</i>&quot;? Do-it-yourself Goblin &quot;Fruit&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1152403-nom-nom-nom?p=1152898#post1152898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no reason for other Refinements to learn how to harvest something from human bodies. Prometheans are natural alchemical furnaces, and humanity is their goal. To process actual humans in several ways seems hardly out of theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but I think only Centimani would be monstrous enough to actually <i>eat</i> people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}